/* book Worked example: Q: A broadcast superhet with a 455 kHz IF and high-side injection is tuned to 1000 kHz. Its RF stage is one tuned circuit with Q = 100. Find fLO, the image and the image rejection. Repeat for a shortwave signal at 25 MHz with the same IF and Q, and with a 1.5 MHz IF.
   1. fLO = 1000 + 455 = 1455 kHz; fsi = 1000 + 2 × 455 = 1910 kHz (check: 1910 − 1455 = 455 kHz).
   2. ρ = 1910/1000 − 1000/1910 = 1.910 − 0.5236 = 1.3864.
   3. α = √(1 + (100 × 1.3864)²) = √(1 + 19 222) = 138.6, that is 20 log 138.6 = 42.8 dB.
   4. 25 MHz: fsi = 25 + 0.91 = 25.91 MHz; ρ = 1.0364 − 0.9649 = 0.0715; α = √(1 + 7.15²) = 7.22, only 17.2 dB.
   5. 1.5 MHz IF at 25 MHz: fsi = 28 MHz; ρ = 1.12 − 0.8929 = 0.2271; α = √(1 + 22.71²) = 22.7, that is 27.1 dB.
   6. Two identical tuned stages at 1000 kHz would give 138.6² = 19 223, or 85.7 dB.
   Answer: fLO = 1455 kHz, fsi = 1910 kHz, α = 138.6 (42.8 dB). At 25 MHz: 7.22 (17.2 dB) with a 455 kHz IF, 22.7 (27.1 dB) with a 1.5 MHz IF. */
