/* book exam traps: Writing fsi = fs + 2fIF for low-side injection. It holds only when the LO is above the signal; with the LO below, fsi = fs − 2fIF. | Saying the IF filter rejects the image. After the mixer the image is already at the IF; only the RF stages can reject it. | Using ρ = (fsi − fs)/fs. The formula is ρ = fsi/fs − fs/fsi: 1.3864, not 0.91, at 1000 kHz. | Adding the dB of two stages wrongly: multiply the ratios (138.6 × 138.6), or add the dB (42.8 + 42.8 = 85.7 dB). */
