/* book Worked example 2: Q: In a basic group, carriers at 64, 68, …, 108 kHz carry 0.3 to 3.4 kHz voice channels as lower sidebands. Find the band of the channels on the 108 kHz and 104 kHz carriers, the gap between them and the band of the whole group.
   1. LSB of a carrier fci: from fci − 3.4 kHz to fci − 0.3 kHz.
   2. 108 kHz carrier: 104.6 to 107.7 kHz. 104 kHz carrier: 100.6 to 103.7 kHz.
   3. Gap: 104.6 − 103.7 = 0.9 kHz, which is the 4 kHz slot minus the 3.1 kHz of speech.
   4. The lowest channel, on 64 kHz, occupies 60.6 to 63.7 kHz. The group spans 60 to 108 kHz: 12 × 4 = 48 kHz.
   Answer: 104.6 to 107.7 kHz and 100.6 to 103.7 kHz, a 0.9 kHz gap; the group occupies 60 to 108 kHz (48 kHz). */
